(a) Design standards. Where required, one or more off-street loading spaces shall be provided on the same or adjoining premises with the facility it serves, either inside or outside a building. A loading berth shall have minimum dimensions of 12 feet by 35 feet by 14 feet overhead clearance. Such facilities must be designed so that no truck or vehicle maneuvering occurs on the public right-of-way nor in areas designated for the parking of vehicles.
(b) Required spaces. The number of spaces or area required for a particular use shall be as follows:
(1) Retail operations, including accessory uses within hotels and office buildings. One loading berth for every 40,000 square feet of floor area or fraction thereof; one loading space for every 20,000 square feet of floor area or fraction thereof;
(2) Office buildings and hotels. One loading berth for every 100,000 square feet of floor area or fraction thereof;
(3) Industrial, manufacturing, distribution and wholesale operations. One loading berth per 50,000 square feet of gross floor area or fraction thereof; and
(4) Hospitals, nursing homes and similar institutions. One loading berth at least then ten feet wide and 30 feet long for each 5,000 square feet of gross floor area or fraction thereof.

